---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { ownerSupplied, placeholderKeys } from "../data/site";

const description =
  "Draft privacy notice for Straight Up Digital, covering what personal information is collected through the website, why, how long it is kept and how to exercise your rights under POPIA.";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy notice"
  description={description}
  canonicalPath="/privacy"
  noindex
>
  <section class="legal">
    <div class="container legal__inner">
      <div class="legal__banner" role="note">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 3l8 4v5c0 5-3.5 8-8 9-4.5-1-8-4-8-9V7l8-4Z"></path><path d="M12 8v4M12 15v.5"></path></svg>
        <p>
          <strong>Draft for review.</strong> This notice has not been approved by a
          lawyer and is not final. It is published as a working draft so the
          wording can be reviewed against POPIA before the site collects real
          enquiries.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h1>Privacy notice</h1>
      <p class="legal__meta">Version privacy-draft-2026-11 · Last updated 13 November 2026</p>

      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          This notice explains what personal information Straight Up Digital
          collects through this website, why it is collected, who it is shared
          with and what you can ask us to do with it. It is written to be read,
          not to hide behind.
        </p>

        <h2>1. Who is responsible</h2>
        <p>
          The responsible party is <strong>Straight Up Digital</strong>. The
          registered legal entity name, registration number and registered address
          are still to be confirmed.
        </p>
        <div class="placeholder-note" data-placeholder={placeholderKeys.legalEntity}>
          <strong>Owner to supply:</strong> legal entity name, registration number
          and registered address.
        </div>
        <p>
          Privacy questions and requests can be sent through the{" "}
          <a href="/contact">enquiry form</a> until a dedicated privacy contact is
          published.
        </p>

        <h2>2. What we collect</h2>
        <p>When you submit an enquiry or audit request, we collect:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Your name, if you provide it.</li>
          <li>Your business name and website address.</li>
          <li>Your email address and, if you choose to provide it, your phone number.</li>
          <li>The service you are interested in and the message you write.</li>
          <li>The date and time you gave consent, and the version of this notice you agreed to.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          The web host also records standard technical information such as the IP
          address, browser type and pages requested, in server logs used for
          security and troubleshooting.
        </p>
        <p>
          We do not ask for identity numbers, card details, passwords or special
          personal information through this website. Please do not send them.
        </p>

        <h2>3. Why we collect it</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>To read and respond to your enquiry.</li>
          <li>To prepare an audit, quote or proposal you have asked for.</li>
          <li>To deliver work you have agreed to and to keep the records the law requires.</li>
          <li>To keep the website secure and prevent abuse of the forms.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Under POPIA, we rely on your consent for the enquiry, on the steps needed
          to prepare or perform a contract, and on our legitimate interest in
          running a secure website. You can withdraw consent at any time by asking
          us to delete your enquiry.
        </p>

        <h2>4. Who we share it with</h2>
        <p>
          We do not sell personal information. We share it only with service
          providers that help run the website and the business:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Netlify</strong> — website hosting and form submission
            handling.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>An email provider</strong> — used to deliver enquiries to the
            business inbox. The provider has not been selected yet.
          </li>
          <li>
            Professional advisers or authorities, where the law requires it.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Some providers may process information outside South Africa. Where that
          happens, we require protections that are at least equivalent to POPIA.
        </p>

        <h2>5. How long we keep it</h2>
        <p>
          Enquiries are kept only as long as needed to respond, to deliver any work
          agreed, and to meet record-keeping obligations. A fixed retention period
          has not been approved yet.
        </p>
        <div class="placeholder-note">
          <strong>Owner to confirm:</strong> the retention period for enquiries,
          quotes and client records, and how records are deleted.
        </div>

        <h2>6. Cookies and analytics</h2>
        <p>
          This site does not set advertising or tracking cookies. Analytics is
          switched off until a privacy-friendly tool is chosen and approved. If
          analytics is enabled later, this notice will say which tool is used and
          the site will ask for consent where the law requires it.
        </p>
        <div class="placeholder-note" data-placeholder={placeholderKeys.analytics}>
          <strong>Owner to confirm:</strong> the analytics tool (or a decision to
          use none) and the cookie notice wording.
        </div>

        <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
        <p>Under POPIA you may ask to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Be told what personal information we hold about you.</li>
          <li>Correct information that is wrong or out of date.</li>
          <li>Delete information we no longer have a lawful reason to keep.</li>
          <li>Object to processing based on legitimate interest.</li>
          <li>Withdraw consent for future processing.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Send the request through the <a href="/contact">enquiry form</a> and say
          what you want us to do. We may need to confirm your identity before
          acting. If you are not satisfied with our response, you may complain to
          the Information Regulator (South Africa).
        </p>

        <h2>8. Security</h2>
        <p>
          Access to enquiries is limited to the people who need it to respond and
          deliver the work. The website is served over HTTPS, and form submissions
          are validated before they are accepted. No system is perfectly secure,
          but we take reasonable steps to protect what you send.
        </p>

        <h2>9. Children</h2>
        <p>
          The website is intended for businesses and is not directed at children.
          We do not knowingly collect information from anyone under 18.
        </p>

        <h2>10. Changes</h2>
        <p>
          When this notice changes, the version date at the top changes too. If the
          change affects how consent works, the form will point to the new version
          before it is submitted.
        </p>

        <h2>11. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          For any privacy question, use the <a href="/contact">enquiry form</a> and
          mark the message “Privacy”. The Information Officer’s name and direct
          details will be published once confirmed.
        </p>
        <div class="placeholder-note" data-placeholder={placeholderKeys.informationOfficer}>
          <strong>Owner to supply:</strong> the Information Officer’s name and
          contact details, as required by POPIA.
        </div>
        {
          ownerSupplied.informationOfficer && (
            <p>Information Officer: {ownerSupplied.informationOfficer}</p>
          )
        }
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
